{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(With_two_different_endings)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (With two different endings)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Coordinates)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Coordinates)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(interesting)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (interesting)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A square with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is inscribed in an isosceles triangle with one side of the square along the base of the triangle. A square with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has two vertices on the other square and the other two on sides of the triangle, as shown. What is the area of the triangle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/0/ee0b3c17b58c14762d6dcde965da0aa09a9cdd3a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] //diagram by kante314  draw((0,0)--(8,0)--(4,8)--cycle, linewidth(1.5));  draw((2,0)--(2,4)--(6,4)--(6,0)--cycle, linewidth(1.5));  draw((3,4)--(3,6)--(5,6)--(5,4)--cycle, linewidth(1.5)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/7/827f02c486a6d87d488429cf6f1214f197aa18d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\textbf{A})\\: 19\\frac14\\qquad(\\textbf{B}) \\: 20\\frac14\\qquad(\\textbf{C}) \\: 21 \\frac34\\qquad(\\textbf{D}) \\: 22\\frac12\\qquad(\\textbf{E}) \\: 23\\frac34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"451\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's split the triangle down the middle and label it:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/0/c906fe16c95e07afb9d864e41b10b071a70b48a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  import olympiad; pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,I,J,K; A = origin; B = (0.5,0); C=(2.5,0); D=(3,0); E = (0.5,2); F=(0.83333333333,2); G=(2.166666666667,2); H=(2.5,2); I=(0.83333333333,3.333333333333); J=(2.166666666667,3.3333333333); K=(1.5,6); draw(A--D--K--cycle); draw(B--E); draw(C--H); draw(F--I); draw(G--J); draw(I--J); draw(E--H); draw(K--(1.5,0)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(1.5,0),S); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(1.5,2),SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(1.5,3.3333333),SW); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,H,SE); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,J,SE); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,K,N);    [/asy]\" width=\"128\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/7/327e0ea8dd5d12473100572af2c584a05200019f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup ADG \\sim \\bigtriangleup BEG \\sim \\bigtriangleup CFG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"229\" height=\"18\" /> by AA similarity. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/4/654e0f7ee0fde8cf55e4f8d9b5fb31fc1e5a4e1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE =  \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11fca7fa0396390456782405b2897976a413f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> cuts the side length of the square in half; similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/9/db920c16c37f9ecd5503cc0b8f06f924bc6f9ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/c/e0cd4c6d0f4501faafcf073309673eb7c9338e83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CG = h$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />: then by side ratios,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/3/b531469f9e967f6a9e3c9db2f9279b6a477322a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{h+2}{h} =  \\frac{\\frac{3}{2}}{1} \\implies 2(h+2) = 3h \\implies h = 4\\]\" width=\"334\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Now the height of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/3/f438209779cde32c0fb105e9f3f134f97992d7be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG = 4+2+3 =  9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"159\" height=\"16\" />. By side ratios, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3cfaf7bd5bdb2b9a1c62bd92c0797a137814c2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{9}{4} = \\frac{AD}{1} \\implies AD = \\frac{9}{4}\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"37\" />. \n</p><p>The area of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/f/32fca2dab4c8ba249951b84e2b72d89e02bc15a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG\\cdot AD = 9 \\cdot \\frac{9}{4}  = \\frac{81}{4} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }20 \\frac{1}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"280\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~KingRavi\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By similarity, the height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc0cca5fb9eb6b212bb853172bb5d076f80b2711.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+\\frac31\\cdot2=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"102\" height=\"38\" /> and the base is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/0/810dd4a5f897e6b71bf85cb6edeed0d3a533242b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac92\\cdot1=4.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"85\" height=\"38\" />. \nThus the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/f/d4f470ba61d457a08d1e37127359727d4fa5c014.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9\\cdot4.5}2=20.25=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }20 \\frac{1}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"219\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Hefei417, or 陆畅 Sunny from China\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28With_two_different_endings.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(With_two_different_endings)\">Solution 3 (With two different endings)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (With two different endings)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This solution is based on this figure: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2021_AMC_10B_(Nov)_Problem_13,_sol.png\" title=\"File:2021 AMC 10B (Nov) Problem 13, sol.png\">Image:2021_AMC_10B_(Nov)_Problem_13,_sol.png</a>\n</p><p>Denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/e/0ae7e617e4e709e7c303643f03c7d399bea88cd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FG = 3$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b103fb96e433214932d2955a12a0e0e759310154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JK = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/3761b0c4ebc6092283eb7839c3a95c9a396d32dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FJ = KG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb856d1760679626648dce563867f5315a8d85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FJ = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"65\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>We observe <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/b/03bad14b3fe0cd18bb9542ff8cafad2e92e097c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADF \\sim \\triangle FJH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />.\nHence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/2/3e2eebab36ba97de050c8a084695bc8174b884a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AD}{FJ} = \\frac{FD}{HJ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"39\" />.\nHence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccfa93c535778d89d945225d304b7dc2140f3abe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = \\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" />.\nBy symmetry, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/9/8991a05f77448b62f6db01a87e2ba74fbffaa493.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE = AD = \\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"122\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76ebb4f22891ad96ee9e724dd087e04214b04995.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AD + DE + BE = \\frac{9}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"225\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/a/dcac1e4ba7f6501820a8265154193f93b4ce0ace.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO = \\frac{9}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"67\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>We observe <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/f/3df058af9c41ce0f2d9e554f4449abb0e03bb7da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AOC \\sim \\triangle ADF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />.\nHence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b54adcd9340b824100f661ff6db366029da8629.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{OC}{DF} = \\frac{AO}{AD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"39\" />.\nHence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/9/439135ec837064a6f8130c4badc33c1f4db54251.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f373f67521f7a7eae01108e3730befeda8e6ef9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\rm Area} \\ \\triangle ABC = \\frac{1}{2} AB \\cdot OC = \\frac{81}{4} = 20 \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"313\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/2/2b23fa1b9bdd2212360eb18a7068a3273891f680.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }20 \\frac{1}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"79\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Alternatively, we can find the height in a slightly different way.\n</p><p>Following from our finding that the base of the large triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/7/647536986001e7f9d574a8e5f7c0b4a32f4fd508.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = \\frac{9}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"67\" height=\"38\" />, we can label the length of the altitude of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/f/ebfcc3eb8e528f00b921f184d291f3ea096a06f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{CHI}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5acb351b7fdc9db8d1c6bbc4d152c9d8d440158d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{CHI} \\sim \\triangle{CAB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/e/10ebc9f4fedd3850508cbc48962086ef281a40b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{HI}{AB} = \\frac{x}{CO}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"39\" />. Substituting and simplifying, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e730cdce7387ae745dc7bb72bcd79f859b350221.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{HI}{AB} = \\frac{x}{CO} \\Rightarrow \\frac{2}{\\frac{9}{2}} = \\frac{x}{x+5} \\Rightarrow \\frac{x}{x+5} = \\frac{4}{9} \\Rightarrow x = 4 \\Rightarrow CO = 4 + 5 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"542\" height=\"46\" />. Therefore, the area of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/1/36172ecae8814aca1b0c96eb9e2f28dfb5d27cbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{9}{2} \\cdot 9}{2} = \\frac{81}{4} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }20 \\frac{1}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"187\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~mahaler\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Coordinates.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Coordinates)\">Solution 4 (Coordinates)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Coordinates)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For convenience, we will use the image provided in the third solution.\n</p><p>We can set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> as the origin.\n</p><p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/e/0ae7e617e4e709e7c303643f03c7d399bea88cd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FG = 3$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b103fb96e433214932d2955a12a0e0e759310154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JK = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>We subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/3926a81a9db71d9566f1f34318868691c7f535b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JK$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/3951902c11a1cd39a091ea15f0f06cbc79095de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/e/7be482ece3fd5175a6a924a029f59d184856f35a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KG = FJ = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"120\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/8/e583e023116c58ffc4cf6727c8117855d8b39d0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HIKJ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> is a square, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/12955908746b54370d77f918fc2fea6d435289eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IK = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Using rise over run, we find that the slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/e/a3e4582dfa9d52de8b89dff6544ad0f56d468604.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-2}{0.5} = -4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbb8858b7eefd40608ac2c33f75f1c80b800bc74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. We plug this in to get the equation of the line that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> runs along: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/5/2c59e59f71195552edca6f9f4135c69b14a6b419.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y = -4x + 9\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" /> \n</p><p>We know that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/e/1ce51ae0c91d3e059f82ba811950d1537aad4661.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-value$\" width=\"76\" height=\"12\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Using this, we find that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/4/fb42d66551f8bd511b3e74ee9541d1a45b761fd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y-value$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. So the coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2c4f68685bbbae2fd8629abc7545d2b8af69f38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>This gives us the height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e5170b3a48d96da708932026f0e94194f415b0b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACB$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/e/94e560007b537fd37e71f11771924ef77b6b8d94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CO = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Now we need to find the coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We know that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/4/fb42d66551f8bd511b3e74ee9541d1a45b761fd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y-value$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Plugging this in, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/c/a7c8c692eb3a31f19bb971d920841d671683fe41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 = -4x +9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da3a84dbebd8c9729337a95b1d61bdf439039386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{4} = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/0/a7027481d7dc6c1cadf691354f19d82e21644eec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{9}{4}, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"46\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e5170b3a48d96da708932026f0e94194f415b0b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACB$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is symmetrical along <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/d/e9dc4f9abdac55c081c747fd2db62ae369497f05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CO$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, we can multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/d/e9dc4f9abdac55c081c747fd2db62ae369497f05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CO$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0964c9cf406ef8e5ec8beaa6a92125f2d8f90460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d7382d4a7e083285679ab9ea1b8f1b3b38e635f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9 \\cdot \\frac{9}{4} = \\frac{81}{4}\\]\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Simplifying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/2/2b23fa1b9bdd2212360eb18a7068a3273891f680.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }20 \\frac{1}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"79\" height=\"49\" /> for the area.\n</p><p>~Achelois\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28interesting.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(interesting)\">Solution 5 (interesting)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (interesting)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call the right triangle to the right of the square with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />. Similarly, call the triangle to the right of the square with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />. Label the ENTIRE triangle triangle ABC. We notice AA similarity between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />. Additionally, the base of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> must have a length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192b4a258ee998961a99523fd0f0a029f9ea194a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.5$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />, because the middle square takes up a length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the other length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> must be evenly split between the two congruent triangles next to the square, being all situated on a length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We then see that the ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b3714d1977e2e6fa2c03536bd04eabab371fd18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" /> must hold for the base of triangle ABC. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/4/c14d8ae13ba87811b7081a9bee0fd695ff39b33b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3:x = 2:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" />, and we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/3/8d3f56dd6373415b932ab99e82c6c2aa08a013a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />. The length of the base is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/8/6b862144504f5019d1e7f4f4e54219e6506ff883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5 + 3 = 9/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We can then find the height of the triangle by thinking about a geometrical sequence. It must be possible that you could continue inscribing squares in the triangles that are made, as every triangle created is similar to the one before it. Using this, we have the geometrical sequence of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f22ec41bcad38dcee4113501f34c29852217ec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 2 + 4/3 +...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" /> (for each side length is the height that is being added) Using the geometrical sequence formula, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22b60fe8bba1de7db16f120e1135d2e647211879.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{1 - \\frac{2}{3}}= \\frac{3}{\\frac{1}{3}} = 3\\cdot3= 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"175\" height=\"45\" />. The height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> whilst the base length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/d/5adcd622a1ba9d557e1e14b7810cd5852e5ec05e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, and multiplying both values and dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/6/1b63d5ef228724391e26df6e4fd0d7a5575386aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9(9)}{2(2)} = 81/4 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }20 \\frac{1}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"200\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~ martianrunner (i do NOT know how to latex)~RandomMathGuy500 (latex)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mq4e-s9ENas\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mq4e-s9ENas</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gxZE3cscswo\">https://youtu.be/gxZE3cscswo</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Uh5Umekq4A8\">https://youtu.be/Uh5Umekq4A8</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/R7TwXgAGYuw?t=639\">https://youtu.be/R7TwXgAGYuw?t=639</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.p